   Career Construction Theory (CCT). This paper introduces a course
   designed to enhance students' career readiness by incorporating Agile
   methodologies for soft skills development, proficiency in modern
   technologies like Large Language Models (LLMs), and targeted career
   preparation such as resume building. The course's effectiveness,
   evaluated through CCT adaptability for 42 students, shows a positive
   impact on career preparedness in three of the four dimensions. This is
   the first attempt to measure the impact of a capstone course on career
   development using CCT adaptability. While the initial results are
   promising, further research is crucial to fully enhance all dimensions
   of CCT adaptability and to explore the scalability of this study across
   other engineering fields, potentially transforming engineering education
   and career preparation on a broader scale.},
